      <div type="clause" n="39.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 39.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="516" ed="#liebermann"/>Ki tort<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#LeisWl_39-1.lnote.oe.6"/> eslevera u faus jugement fra pur curruz [u<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#LeisWl_39-1.lnote.oe.7"/>] pur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#LeisWl_39-1.lnote.oe.8"/> hange u pur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#LeisWl_39-1.lnote.oe.8"/> aveir, seit en la<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#LeisWl_39-1.lnote.oe.9"/> forfaiture<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#LeisWl_39-1.lnote.oe.10"/> le rei de<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#LeisWl_39-1.lnote.oe.11"/> XL solz, s’il ne pot aleier, que<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#LeisWl_39-1.lnote.oe.2"/> plus dreit faire<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#LeisWl_39-1.lnote.oe.12"/> nel so[u]t<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#LeisWl_39-1.lnote.oe.13"/>; si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#LeisWl_39-1.lnote.oe.b"/> perde sa franchise, si al rei nel pot reachater<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#LeisWl_39-1.lnote.oe.14"/> a soun pleisir.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="516" ed="#liebermann"/>Qui uero falsum iudicium fecerit uel iniustitiam fouerit odio uel amore uel peccunia, sit in regis forisfacto de XL solid., nisi purgare se possit, quod melius iudicare nesciuit; et insuper libertatem, si habuit, amittat illam, nisi a rege eam redemerit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="39.1" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="270" ed="#robertson"/>Ki tort eslevera u faus jugement fra pur curruz [u] pur hange u pur aveir, seit en la forfaiture le rei de XL solz, s'il ne pot aleier que plus dreit faire nel so[u]t; si perde sa franchise, si al rei nel pot reachater a soun plaisir.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="516" ed="#liebermann"/>39, 1. Wer Unrecht aufstellt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_39-1.lnote.de.1"/> oder falsches Urtheil fällt aus Zorn oder aus Hass oder für Geld, sei in Busse [zu Gunsten] des Königs von 40 Schill.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#LeisWl_39-1.lnote.de1.a"/> — wenn er nicht beeiden kann, dass er es nicht richtiger zu fällen verstand — und verliere sein [Gerichtsbarkeits]privileg<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#LeisWl_39-1.lnote.de1.b"/>, wenn er es nicht vom König wieder auslösen kann nach dessen Belieben.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">39, 1. Whoever sets up wrong or pronounces false judgement out of anger or out of hatred or for money shall be liable to a compensation [in favour] of the king of 40 shill. — if he cannot swear that he did not understand how to pronounce it more rightly — and shall lose his [jurisdictional] privilege, unless he can redeem it again from the king at the latter's pleasure.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="271" ed="#robertson"/>He who promotes injustice or pronounces an unjust judgment, as the result of rage or malice or bribery, shall forfeit 40 shillings to the King, unless he can declare on oath that he did not know how to act more justly; he shall lose his right of jurisdiction, unless it be the King's pleasure to allow him to redeem it.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="516">II Cn 15.1[?]</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 15, 1[?]</note>
        <note type="comparisonIncomplete">Some of Liebermann’s notes here are cut off in the gutter of the scan used, and are still to be completed.</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_13">Leis Wl 13</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 270–271 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 516, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_39-1.lnote.oe.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">516</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> et <hi rend="italic">aus L Cnut</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read et from L Cnut</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_39-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">516</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">qui <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">qui Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_39-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">516</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">tozt <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">tozt Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_39-1.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">516</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ne <hi rend="italic">I; gebessert Palgrave</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ne I; corrected by Palgrave</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_39-1.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">516</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">per <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">per Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_39-1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">516</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">missing in Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_39-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">516</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">forsaunre <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">forsaunre Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_39-1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">516</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">d’ <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">d’ Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_39-1.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">516</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fair <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fair Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_39-1.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">516</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sont <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sont I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_39-1.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">516</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">rach. a son plaisir <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">rach. a son plaisir Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_39-1.lnote.de1.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">516</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">die</hi> 120 scil. <hi rend="italic">Cnuts rechnet Verf. hier zu je</hi> ⅓ <hi rend="italic">Normannischen, also als Mercische; vgl. dagegen u.</hi> 42, 1. <hi rend="italic">Er widerspricht o.</hi> 13</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">the author here reckons Cnut’s 120 scil. at ⅓ of a Norman shilling each, i.e. as Mercian ones; cf., on the other hand, below 42, 1. He contradicts above 13</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_39-1.lnote.de1.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">516</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">persönliche Freiheit <hi rend="italic">missverstanden Frühere;</hi> libertatem <hi rend="italic">erklärt L durch seinen Zusatz als</hi> Privileg; <hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> 42, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘personal freedom’ is a misunderstanding of earlier editors; L explains libertatem by his addition as privilege; cf. 42, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_39-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">291</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Unrecht tun’ zu schwach Schmid; eher ‘fördert [Amtsvergehen verübend], obsiegen lässt’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Schmid’s ‘does wrong’ is too weak; rather ‘furthers [committing misconduct in office], lets prevail’</seg></note>
      </div>
